This is how food items are marked as rotten (orotten = TRUE):

Fortune cookies are never 'rotten'.
Cursed non-corpse food is always 'rotten'.
1 in 7 (all if already marked as rotten) non-corpse food is 'rotten' if 
it's old (over 30/60 (U/B) game ticks[1]).
1 in 7 (all if already marked as rotten) non-lizard and -lichen corpses 
are 'rotten' unless:
It was so old that it was tainted.
It was acidic and you are not acid resistant.
4 out of 5 poisonous corpses.
It made you sick.

(BUC-status of a corpse affects the chance that the corpse is tainted or 
makes you sick.)

Now if the food item is 'rotten' it can make you confused, blind or pass 
out. If it makes you pass out the food item is marked as rotten. So 
every food item markes as rotten is also partially eaten.

As is already noted elsewhere in this thread ages (in game ticks[1]) of 
different same type food items are averaged when merged. The difference 
in ages doesn't prohibit the merge. And if you re-read my comments on 
mergable() it doesn't even check the age-field for food items.

Topi

[1] Game ticks in NetHack is counted using the variable monstermoves as 
the speed of the hero doesn't affect this. As the age-field normally has 
the creation time (in monstermoves) of the object, monstermoves-o.age 
gives the age of the item o.
